{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271116-does-worship-by-the-immaculate-order-give-spirits-a-cult-background-second-edition","id":1271116,"title":"Does worship by the immaculate order give spirits a cult background?(second edition)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-27T07:05:52-08:00","id":1271116,"title":"Does worship by the immaculate order give spirits a cult background?(second edition)","content":"It appears even a fairly important loyalist god such as gri-fel only has a cult rating of 1.<br /> Also i always took it for granted that the ban on illegal &quot;prayers&quot; to gods only applies to sacrifices right? It's not illegal to say &quot;bless the god of peach/medicine/health&quot; right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T07:11:59-08:00","id":1271120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271116-does-worship-by-the-immaculate-order-give-spirits-a-cult-background-second-edition#post1271116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears even a fairly important loyalist god such as gri-fel only has a cult rating of 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, that's odd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also i always took it for granted that the ban on illegal &quot;prayers&quot; to gods only applies to sacrifices right? It's not illegal to say &quot;bless the god of peach/medicine/health&quot; right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's quite the way that worship in Exalted would be expressed anyway, but no, the Immaculate Order maintains a calendar of festival days on which the monks will worship specific spirits. Higher ranking and more important gods alternately get more days on the calendar or more widespread ceremonies. Overall, the worship from that is still sufficient to provide a Cult Background of the appropriate level.<br /> <br /> In terms of Yu-Shan, many gods are going to want prayer in excess of their allotments even if it doesn't change their dot rating, because extra prayers give them extra ambrosia. In a lot of cases, probably not enough to change their Salary rating, but hey, if you found a note for one hundred units of your relevant currency lying on the ground, you wouldn't turn out down, would you? Even if it's not exactly making you meaningfully richer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T07:17:38-08:00","id":1271122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271116-does-worship-by-the-immaculate-order-give-spirits-a-cult-background-second-edition?p=1271120#post1271120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really, that's odd.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure that's quite the way that worship in Exalted would be expressed anyway, but no, the Immaculate Order maintains a calendar of festival days on which the monks will worship specific spirits. Higher ranking and more important gods alternately get more days on the calendar or more widespread ceremonies. Overall, the worship from that is still sufficient to provide a Cult Background of the appropriate level.<br /> <br /> In terms of Yu-Shan, many gods are going to want prayer in excess of their allotments even if it doesn't change their dot rating, because extra prayers give them extra ambrosia. In a lot of cases, probably not enough to change their Salary rating, but hey, if you found a note for one hundred units of your relevant currency lying on the ground, you wouldn't turn out down, would you? Even if it's not exactly making you meaningfully richer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do terrestrial gods lack a salary background cause the concept was introduced later or are they actually not getting paid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T07:26:16-08:00","id":1271127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271116-does-worship-by-the-immaculate-order-give-spirits-a-cult-background-second-edition?p=1271122#post1271122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do terrestrial gods lack a salary background cause the concept was introduced later or are they actually not getting paid?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's mostly not getting paid. There are complications written into the function of quintessence and ambrosia around them disappearing if you take them out of Yu-Shan or a god's sanctum (which I think they can only get to if carried by a god via the right magic), but I'd say those were written in for reasons including reinforcing that Terrestrial gods don't really get paid like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}